# 018-embedded-proxy — Completion Report

Completed: 2026-05-27

## What was implemented

### New files

**`internal/proxy/balancer.go`**
- `RoundRobinDirector` struct with thread-safe RWMutex-guarded IP pool
- `WatchDNS(ctx, host, interval)` — background ticker that polls `net.DefaultResolver.LookupHost` to keep the pool fresh (bypassing Go's DNS cache)
- `DirectRequest(req)` — atomic `sync/atomic.AddUint64` counter for lockless index stepping across live endpoints
- `SetIPs` / `IPs` helpers for testing and pool replacement

**`internal/proxy/proxy.go`**
- `BlocklistChecker` interface — satisfied by `cache.BlocklistCache` (`IsBlockedWithExpiration`)
- `AccountingProcessor` interface — satisfied by `accounting.Engine` (`Process`, `BuildEntityKey`)
- `Metrics` struct — three Prometheus families registered against the shared `*prometheus.Registry`:
  - `drl_proxy_requests_total` (labels: host, route, status)
  - `drl_proxy_errors_total` (labels: host, route, reason)
  - `drl_proxy_latency_seconds` histogram (labels: host, route)
- `Server` — built on `net/http/httputil.ReverseProxy` + `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5`
  - `Start(ctx)` — starts plain HTTP (`ListenAndServe`) or TLS (`ListenAndServeTLS`) depending on `tls.enabled`; shuts down gracefully on ctx cancellation
  - `buildRouter(ctx)` — constructs chi.Mux with one handler per `host × route` combination
  - `buildReverseProxy(ctx, hostname, route)` — standard Director for single upstreams; `RoundRobinDirector`-backed Director when `balance-strategy = "dns-round-robin"`
  - `rateLimitMiddleware` — checks blocklist before forwarding, fires async `accounting.Process` after; returns 429 on blocked entities
  - `buildTLSConfig(cfg)` — base64-decodes inline PEM cert and key, loads via `crypto/tls.X509KeyPair`; no disk writes

**`internal/proxy/balancer_test.go`** (7 tests)
- Empty pool leaves URL unchanged
- Single-IP pool always targets that IP
- Multi-IP pool distributes across all addresses
- Atomic counter correctness under 50 concurrent goroutines (race detector)
- `SetIPs` replaces the pool atomically
- Missing-port fallback to `:80` (HTTP) and `:443` (HTTPS)

**`internal/proxy/proxy_test.go`** (7 tests)
- Invalid base64 cert → error with `"decode base64 cert"`
- Invalid base64 key → error with `"decode base64 key"`
- Valid base64 but bad PEM → error with `"parse X509 key pair"`
- Valid self-signed cert/key round-trip → `tls.Config` with one certificate, TLS 1.2 minimum
- Virtual-host isolation: request to `/a/*` reaches backend A, `/b/*` reaches backend B
- Blocked entity returns HTTP 429
- Allowed entity passes through to upstream (HTTP 200)
- Prometheus metrics families present and observable after first observation
- `nil` registry → server usable with `metrics == nil`

### Modified files

**`internal/config/config.go`**
- Added `EmbeddedProxyConfig` (fields: `Enabled`, `Listen`, `TLS`, `Hosts`) wired into `Config` struct as `embedded-proxy` KDL stanza with `DRL_EMBEDDED_PROXY_` env prefix
- Added `EmbeddedProxyTLSConfig` (`Enabled`, `Cert`, `Key`)
- Added `ProxyHostConfig` — positional `,arg` for hostname, nested `ProxyRoutesWrapper`
- Added `ProxyRoutesWrapper` — slice of `ProxyRouteConfig` under `kdl:"route"`
- Added `ProxyRouteConfig` — `Prefix` (positional arg), `Upstream`, `BalanceStrategy`, `DNSRefreshInterval`, `RequireAuth`
- Extended `GetConfigSection` to handle `"embedded-proxy"`

**`internal/config/resources/default.kdl`**
- Added `embedded-proxy` block with `enabled false`, `listen ":8443"`, and a `tls { enabled false }` sub-block

**`go.mod` / `go.sum`**
- Added `github.com/go-chi/chi/v5 v5.3.0`

## Verification

- `mise run lint` — 0 issues
- `mise run test` — all 424 tests pass across 10 packages (proxy package: 16/16 PASS, 54.2% coverage)
